    "result_text": "Both parts of the change are in, and `bin/e2e` now passes all 4 tests. Before my changes, 3 of the 4 failed.\n\n**Carried figure fixed on close**\n- Closing, soft-closing or auto-closing a period now saves each person's carried figure for it, alongside their period due-total. It's worked out on the server the same way the screen works it out live.\n- Reopening a period deletes the saved figures, so the carried figure is live again.\n- The figures are stored in a new table, `period_person_carried`, created by the migration `V78__period_person_carried.sql`. The `Period` entity and the periods API response now include them.\n- On screen (`features/periods/periods.ts`), a closed or soft-closed period shows the saved carried figure. A person added after the close shows `0.00`.\n\n**Consolidated figures as of a date**\n- While an as-of date is set, the consolidated people count, due-total and overdue-total now read the sheet and every descendant as it stood at the end of that day, with that date as each sheet's today. Before, they always showed the store as it is now.\n- Which sheets count as the tree still comes from the parent links as they are now. A sheet whose parent was set after the as-of date is still included, read as of that date. The request doesn't say which way this should go, and the tests pass with this choice.",
